P = {
# ── resource_liquidation: the Overseer sells the shelter piece by piece ──
"quest_resource_liquidation_01": ("The Overseer needs trade capital, and the first seizure order names spare parts: everything not currently installed is now inventory, and a list of currently installed has been drawn up. The mechanic has read the list and says half the machines are kept alive by the parts on it, and the Overseer's office has thanked him for the correction.",
 "The mechanic stands at the parts shelf with the inventory form, filling it in slowly, and some of the lines he leaves blank.",
 "Hand over the spare parts.", "Hide the parts. Falsify the list."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_02": ("The second order names filters: all surplus air and water filters are to be liquidated for trade capital. Surplus is defined as one per sector, and the shelter has learned what one per sector means during storm season, and the order was written by a man whose office has three.",
 "The filter shelf has been counted twice and the counts disagree, and the quartermaster has chosen the smaller number.",
 "Liquidate the surplus filters.", "Log every filter as in use."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_03": ("The order has moved to personal property: heirloom jewelry is dead weight, the notice says, and the trade caravans pay in grain by the gram. People have been asked to surrender rings and watches with a receipt and an apology, and the man writing the receipts has started apologizing twice, and has been replaced.",
 "A woman stands at the surrender table with her hand closed around something, and the receipt waits, and her hand stays closed.",
 "Collect the heirlooms.", "Refuse the order. Some things are not capital."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_04": ("The Overseer's office has priced the shelter's library: history books weigh paper, and the caravans take it. The settlement's history fits in two crates. The librarian has been asked to choose which, and has handed in a list of the titles he would burn first, and the list is blank, and he refuses to correct it.",
 "The librarian stands before the shelves with packing crates, and has spent the morning re-shelving books that did not need re-shelving.",
 "Crates of books for trade.", "Bury the library instead. Dig it up later."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_05": ("The order defines enough: one set of clothes per person, and the extras are collected, baled, and sold, and enough is counted at inspection. Winter is two months off, and the notice says trade capital buys grain now, and grain is calories, and the arithmetic is at the bottom and it is confident and it is wrong.",
 "The inspection line moves past the bale tables wearing everything it owns at once, and the inspector has been told not to comment.",
 "Enforce the collection.", "Cancel the inspection."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_06": ("The seizure reaches bedding: blankets, mattresses, whatever stands between the floor and a person. The caravans pay well for cloth. The order promises replacements when capital allows, and the shelter has heard the word when before, and the infirmary has started counting coughs in advance.",
 "The bedding room door is locked, and the quartermaster has the key, and the quartermaster is nowhere anyone will say.",
 "Seize the bedding.", "Bar the bedding room."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_07": ("The order reaches the dispensary: medicine is trade capital now, and the caravans pay in grain for what is in the bottles. The medical officer has been asked to price each shelf, and has written not for sale on every line, and has been asked again, and has written it smaller.",
 "The dispensary price sheet is posted with not for sale in a column, in very small letters, all the way down.",
 "Price the medicine and sell it.", "Post the sheet as it stands."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_08": ("The order has come to a stop, and the settlement has stopped with it: the caravans have offered a price, and the Overseer's office has written it down, and the words used are wardship transfer, and the price is grain, and it is not small. The notice has been posted, removed, and posted again, and nobody knows who keeps posting it.",
 "The notice stands on the wall again, and a crowd stands in front of it, and nobody speaks, and nobody leaves.",
 "Approve the transfers.", "Burn the notice. Guard the dormitory."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_09": ("There is no polite version of the order, and the Overseer's office has tried anyway: the sick carry harvestable capital, and the grain offered for it would feed the shelter through winter, and the arithmetic is on the notice, and next to the arithmetic someone has written the word no, and nobody knows who, and nobody wants to.",
 "The infirmary door is barred from the inside, and the medical officer has not come out since the order arrived.",
 "Authorize the harvest.", "Hold the infirmary, whatever it costs."),
"quest_resource_liquidation_10": ("The final order addresses the healthy: blood drawn by the pint and sold to the caravans, and the grain price is listed per person, and the notice calls it donation, and the word is typed where order should be. The line forms at the clinic door, and the line is there to keep people out, not in.",
 "The line at the clinic door is four deep and it is holding the door shut, and the caravan waits outside with its grain.",
 "Open the blood line.", "Send the caravan away. Keep the blood."),
# ── expedition_sacrifices: scout orders climb past every line ──
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_01": ("Surface returns came in light, so the orders have started: scout teams skip sleep until the quotas are met. The first team has been out two days, and their report is legible, and the handwriting gets worse toward the end of it.",
 "The scout lead reads the order twice, folds it, and checks her team's boots. Nobody says anything.",
 "Order them out without sleep.", "Let them sleep. Take the quota hit."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_02": ("The order has been revised upward: scouts carry double loads on the return leg, and the weight was calculated by the operations office, by a man who has never carried a pack. The team has been shown the arithmetic. They laughed once, briefly, and nobody laughs anymore.",
 "The pack frames stand loaded by the airlock, twice as tall as they should be, and nobody has lifted one yet.",
 "Load them double.", "Cut the loads. Run twice instead."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_03": ("The order calls protocol a luxury of the supplied: scout teams ignore radiation limits until quota is met, and dosimeters are collected at the airlock to prevent alarm. The scout lead has asked what happens when someone comes home hot. The operations office has said the dosimeters will tell them.",
 "The dosimeter basket sits by the airlock, and the team walks past it, and nobody reaches for a badge.",
 "Strip the protocols.", "Refuse. The badges go with the team."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_04": ("The forecast shows an ash storm building to the east, and the order says march through it: storms empty the routes of competition, and the quota is time-sensitive. The team has been issued goggles and wet cloths, and the storm has been given a name on the operations board, and the name is Opportunity.",
 "The storm wall stands on the horizon, and the team stands at the airlock, and between them is a line on the map called Opportunity.",
 "Send them into the storm.", "Hold them until it passes."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_05": ("The order has reached the line it was always reaching: teams that take wounded are to leave them with one day's water, because carrying costs quota, and the word used is delays. The team has read the order aloud to each other, once each, so everyone heard it in their own voice.",
 "The team stands in a circle, and nobody looks at anyone else, and somebody cleans a rifle that is already clean.",
 "Confirm the abandonment order.", "Tear it up. Nobody gets left."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_06": ("The operations board has marked a route through the old minefield, because the route is straight and the quota is straight, and the order says walk single file and follow the track of the person ahead. The scout lead has asked who walks first. The operations office has said volunteers. There have been no volunteers, and the silence has been noted.",
 "The minefield line is drawn on the map in red, and the team stands around the table, and every face says the same thing.",
 "Order the crossing.", "Take the long route. Pay the hours."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_07": ("The order forbids weapons as a weight saving: teams engage raiders unarmed rather than lose hours, and the notice says raiders respect numbers, and the team has been asked to walk in close formation and look like more. The scout lead has counted her team out loud, twice, in front of the operations office.",
 "The weapons rack is locked, and the team's pack straps hang empty, and the lock is the quartermaster's.",
 "Send them out unarmed.", "Break the lock. Arm the team."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_08": ("The quotas have moved into the red zone: the salvage there is rich, the readings are rich, and the order lists both columns and totals only one. The team has been issued new filters and old dosimeters, and the dosimeters have been calibrated not to alarm, and someone in operations has initialed that.",
 "The red zone sits on the operations board as a column of figures, and under the figures someone has penciled and back?, and nobody has answered it.",
 "Send the team into the red zone.", "Strike the zone from the board."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_09": ("The order no longer hides its subject: teams resupply from the dead in the field, because the quotas are long-range, and the words on the notice are field protein, and the words are typed. The scout lead has come to the operations office and stood in the doorway a long time without saying anything, and left.",
 "The notice hangs by the airlock, and the team walks past it without reading it, and everyone has read it.",
 "Let the order stand.", "Recall the team. Starve on this side."),
"quest_expedition_sacrifices_10": ("The final order is one line: return with quota or do not return, and the airlock codes have been changed, and the new codes have not been issued to the teams, and the teams know, because the panel will not take their badges. They stand at the door with their packs on, waiting for someone to say the order out loud.",
 "The team stands at the airlock with packs on, and the badge panel blinks red, and nobody from operations has come down to look.",
 "Hold the door until quota returns.", "Open the door. Let them come home."),
# ── water_restriction: the aquifer dies one allowance at a time ──
"quest_water_restriction_01": ("The aquifer gauge has dropped again, and the first cut is showers: washing is suspended until the water returns, and the notice says the body adapts, and the infirmary has added skin rot to its forecasts. The settlement has started washing at the basins with cups, carefully, like a rite.",
 "The shower room is locked, and from behind the basin room comes the sound of one cup of water, and then none.",
 "Cut the showers.", "Ration cups, but keep the washing."),
"quest_water_restriction_02": ("The second cut is laundry: clothes are worn until they stand, and the water saved is logged each day like a victory. The infirmary has started counting what it calls contact complaints, and the count rises with the savings, and the two charts hang side by side, and nobody has noticed, or nobody has said.",
 "Two charts on the infirmary wall: water saved, and contact complaints. The lines cross in week three.",
 "Suspend the laundry.", "Keep the wash-day. Cut somewhere else."),
"quest_water_restriction_03": ("The cut reaches the hydroponics bay: half water, half yield, and the arithmetic is on the notice, and the bay chief has written her arithmetic underneath it, and hers ends in a word the notice does not use, famine, and her arithmetic has been crossed out by someone, and the crossing out has been crossed out again.",
 "The bay chief stands over her rows with a measuring cup, giving each plant half of what it asks for.",
 "Halve the bay's water.", "Keep the bay full. Cut leadership's allowance."),
"quest_water_restriction_04": ("The order has started sorting people: the lower decks take the first cut, because their work is light and their thirst is cheap, and the word lower is printed like a floor number, and it is a floor number, and the people on it have started saying it out loud, slowly, in meetings.",
 "The lower deck's water point has a smaller tap than the one above it now, and the settlement has started calling it by name.",
 "Cut the lower decks first.", "One tap, one line, one measure."),
"quest_water_restriction_05": ("The cut reaches the infirmary: the sick need water least, the notice reasons, because they are not working, and the charge nurse has answered by posting the fever chart on the door, and the chart says what fevers cost in water, and the notice has been taken down by someone, and nobody has put it back.",
 "The fever chart hangs on the infirmary door, and every line on it is a name, and the notice is gone.",
 "Cut the infirmary's allowance.", "Refuse. Fevers are thirst."),
"quest_water_restriction_06": ("The order names ages now: the elderly take a reduced cup, because their years are fewer and the water is finite, and the arithmetic is not written down, because even the notice's author could not bring themselves to write it. The eldest dweller has asked to see the order, and has been shown it, and has read it aloud, and the room has not moved.",
 "The eldest dweller stands with the order in his hands, and he has finished reading it, and nobody takes it back.",
 "Reduce the elderly cup.", "Pour him a full cup. In public."),
"quest_water_restriction_07": ("The cut reaches the children, and the notice calls it smaller cups for smaller people, and nobody who has read it has been able to repeat the sentence, and the schoolroom has started teaching with the door shut. What the teacher teaches in there is not logged, but the children come out quiet, and not frightened, which is worse.",
 "The water point has a step-stool for the children to reach the tap, and somebody has removed the stool.",
 "Issue the smaller cups.", "Put the stool back. Fill their cups first."),
"quest_water_restriction_08": ("The last real order is one sentence: water is issued to leadership only until the aquifer recovers, and the notice calls it stewardship, and the taps on the command deck have locks on them now, and the locksmith has been asked to fit the locks, and has fitted them slowly, and has left his tools behind, and has not come back for them.",
 "The command deck taps are locked, and the locksmith's tools sit under them, and the locksmith is in the line downstairs.",
 "Lock the water to leadership.", "Break the locks. Open every tap."),
"quest_water_restriction_09": ("The order has stopped being about water: complete dehydration protocols are issued, because the body holds reserves, the notice says, and the reserves are listed, and the infirmary has refused to co-sign, and the order has been issued without the signature, and the word experimental appears once, near the bottom.",
 "The protocol is posted, and the infirmary's signature line is blank, and everybody has noticed the blank.",
 "Issue the protocols.", "Burn them. Post the ashes."),
"quest_water_restriction_10": ("The last order is written in engineering language: human waste is to be distilled and returned as drinking water, and the system is designed, and the pipes are requisitioned, and the shelter has gone quiet the way rooms go quiet. The engineers have been asked to build it, and have asked, quietly, who drinks first.",
 "The pipe requisition form sits on the table, and the engineer holds the pen, and the room is waiting for the answer to who drinks first.",
 "Build the system.", "Refuse. Dig for water instead."),
# ── propaganda_control: the office swallows the truth ──
"quest_propaganda_control_01": ("The truth has started causing panic, the office says, so listening hours are now mandatory: one hour a day of the shelter broadcast, attendance logged. The first hour has been held, and the broadcast spoke about reserves, and the reserves are known, and the log was passed around, and everyone signed, and nobody said the word known.",
 "The loudspeaker hangs in the mess hall with the logbook under it, and the hour has started, and the room listens the way you listen to rain.",
 "Mandate the listening hour.", "Cut the speaker's wire."),
"quest_propaganda_control_02": ("The office has found a source of panic: pre-war books, which describe plenty and cause despair, and the ban is issued with a list, and the list is long, and the librarian has been asked to enforce it, and has asked for time, and the time has been granted, and she has spent it reading.",
 "The librarian sits in the archive with the ban list, reading, and the book cart stands empty by the door where the burn pile is meant to be.",
 "Enforce the ban.", "Let her hide them. Sign nothing."),
"quest_propaganda_control_03": ("The shelter's history is being revised: the first days are rewritten to include order, because the truth of the first days causes panic, and the new text has been printed and pasted over the old, and someone has peeled a corner, and under the corner the truth is legible, and the corner has been glued down again by someone, and the glue is fresh.",
 "The history board has new text on it, and one corner is peeling, and the glue pot beside the board is fresh, and nobody admits to either.",
 "Post the new history.", "Peel the corner. Let it read."),
"quest_propaganda_control_04": ("The order has moved inward: references to the before are removed from broadcasts, and school lessons are revised to begin at the exchange, and the word before is discouraged. The children have started asking what the word means, and the teachers have been told not to answer, and one teacher has answered anyway, and has been noted.",
 "A child asks the room what before means, and the room looks at the teacher, and the teacher looks at the notice.",
 "Erase the before.", "Teach the word. Take the note."),
"quest_propaganda_control_05": ("Morale is measured now, and out loud: the settlement gathers daily for the gratitude hour to cheer for the shelter, and attendance is logged, and enthusiasm is observed. The first hour has been held, and the sound it made is a sound the shelter has never made before, and it is not cheering, and it was logged as cheering.",
 "The gratitude hour is held, and the sound goes up, and the observer takes notes, and the notes are positive, and the sound is not.",
 "Hold the gratitude hour.", "Refuse the cheer. Stand silent. Log that."),
"quest_propaganda_control_06": ("The office has discovered the last private place is the family, and the new duty is reporting: dissent in the home is to be reported by whoever hears it. The first report has been filed by a child against a parent, because the child was taught it was a duty, and the office has praised the child publicly, and the settlement has watched the praise, and has learned something it cannot unlearn.",
 "The child stands on the stage receiving praise, and the parent stands in the crowd, and nobody looks at either of them, and everybody does.",
 "Enforce the reporting duty.", "Bury the report. Warn the family."),
"quest_propaganda_control_07": ("The order has crossed its last quiet line: dissent is now corrected publicly, because panic about the truth requires a visible answer, and the first sentence has been read out, and the settlement has been gathered to hear it, and the word used is demonstration, and the settlement has stood for it, and been counted while standing.",
 "The sentence is posted and the hour is set, and the assembly bell has been rung early, so nobody can say they did not hear.",
 "Carry out the demonstration.", "Open the gate. Let the prisoner walk."),
"quest_propaganda_control_08": ("The office has finished its work: the Overseer is now the object of mandatory worship, and the liturgy has been written, and the hour set, and a hymn, and the settlement has been asked to sing, and has sung, and the sound of it is in the log, and the Overseer has asked that the log be read aloud at meals, because faith should be heard.",
 "The hymn is posted by the mess hall door, and the settlement eats in front of it, and nobody sings at meals, and the hour comes anyway.",
 "Hold the worship hour.", "Boil the hymn sheets for fuel."),
"quest_propaganda_control_09": ("The final proposal arrives in medical language: a chemical calm is to be added to the water supply, because panic is an illness and illnesses are treated, and the dosage is listed, and the medical officer has been asked to supervise, and has asked what the calm does to questions, and the office has said the questions are the illness.",
 "The dosage sheet sits by the water tank, and the medical officer stands in front of it with her hand on the valve, and her hand stays there.",
 "Dose the water.", "Drain the tank. Take the blame."),
"quest_propaganda_control_10": ("The last document is calm, which is the horror of it: total mind erasure, voluntary by signature, because memory causes panic and the shelter must be stable. The form is printed, and the forms sit by the water point, and one of them is signed, and the signature is the office clerk, and the clerk is smiling, and nobody remembers what he used to be like.",
 "The forms sit by the water point, and one is signed, and the clerk smiles at everyone, and nobody can say what he lost.",
 "Offer the erasure.", "Burn the forms. And the desk."),
# ── caloric_share: generosity climbs the same ladder ──
"quest_caloric_share_01": ("The deficit is real and the reserves are real, and a proposal has come up from the mess hall floor: open the reserves and share with the hungry first, and count the cost later. The proposal is written on the back of a ration card, and the card has been passed around the room, and the signatures are in order of hunger.",
 "The ration card sits on the council table with signatures on both sides, and the reserve door is unlocked, and nobody has opened it yet.",
 "Open the reserves. Feed them.", "Hold the reserves. Winter is longer than hunger."),
"quest_caloric_share_02": ("The proposal has moved to the infirmary: reserve rations for the sick, because fevers spend the body and the body must be repaid. The medical officer has co-signed it, which she has never done for anything, and the notice has been posted by hand, and the handwriting is steady, and the clinic has started setting out bowls.",
 "The infirmary has set out bowls by the door, and the reserve key is in the medical officer's hand, and the room is waiting on the vote.",
 "Feed the sick from the reserves.", "Hold the reserves. Prescribe what we can."),
"quest_caloric_share_03": ("The proposal names the elderly: reserves for the people who built the shelter, because the debt is old and the winter is new. The eldest dweller has been told, and has asked that the children eat first, and the request has been written into the proposal, and the signatures have grown faster because of it.",
 "The eldest dweller sits at the head of the table with the proposal in front of him, and he has added one line: children first.",
 "Share with the elderly.", "Refuse. The reserves outlast the debt."),
"quest_caloric_share_04": ("The proposal reaches the children's dormitory: reserve rations for the orphans, and the matron has presented the count, and the count is smaller than the room would like, and the proposal asks for double portions because children grow, and the double portion has been seconded by the cook, who has the keys.",
 "The cook stands by the reserve door with the keys, and the count of children is written on the door in chalk, and the chalk is fresh.",
 "Double the children's portions.", "Hold to single portions. For now."),
"quest_caloric_share_05": ("The proposal is quiet this time: reserve rations for the grieving, because grief spends appetite, and the bereaved have been forgetting to eat, and nobody noticed who was not eating until it was written on the proposal card, and the room has gone still while it is read aloud.",
 "The proposal card is read aloud, and the room is still, and somebody stands up and sits back down, and the vote is not called yet.",
 "Bring meals to the bereaved.", "Refuse. Grief is not a ration line."),
"quest_caloric_share_06": ("The proposal names the injured: reserve rations until they heal, because bodies rebuild out of what they are given. The injured have been listed, and the list is longer than the room expected, because injuries have been hidden to keep from burdening the shelter, and the hiding is written into the proposal, and the room goes still again.",
 "The injury list is posted, and half the names are surprises, and the reserve key is on the table, and the vote is close.",
 "Feed the injured until they heal.", "Hold the reserves. Bind them instead."),
"quest_caloric_share_07": ("The proposal reaches its hardest place: reserve rations for the outsiders, the ones taken in from the ash last week, and the room divides the way rooms divide, and the vote is called, and the outsiders are asked to step outside while it happens, and one of them asks, quietly, why.",
 "The outsiders stand by the door, and the room has asked them to step out, and one of them has asked why, and nobody answers.",
 "Feed them. They stay.", "Refuse. The reserves are ours."),
"quest_caloric_share_08": ("The proposal reaches the brig: reserve rations for the prisoners, because the brig's portions were cut last season and the cut was never voted on. The brig keeper has presented the count, and stands in the doorway while he presents it, and says nothing else, and the silence says the rest.",
 "The brig keeper stands in the council doorway with the count in his hands, and he is not asking. He is waiting.",
 "Restore the brig portions.", "Refuse. They eat what is left."),
"quest_caloric_share_09": ("The proposal is last this time: reserve rations for the dying, because the end of a body should not be hunger. The hospice volunteers present it, and the room does not debate it, and the vote passes without a count, and the reserves are opened that evening, and the cook goes herself.",
 "The hospice volunteers stand at the table, and the room does not debate, and the reserve door is already open, and the cook is going through it.",
 "Feed the dying well.", "Refuse. Save it for the living."),
"quest_caloric_share_10": ("The final proposal is one line: total equality, every rank eating the same measure, because the deficit belongs to everyone or no one. The council has been asked to eat last, and the council has read the line aloud, and the room has waited, and the waiting was the vote.",
 "One line is posted by the mess hall door, and it says one measure for all, and the council sits at the end of the line with their plates.",
 "One measure for everyone.", "Keep the ranks. Keep the reserves."),
}
